From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] i2c: mt65xx: Hold a CPU latency request during transfers

Every message of a transfer waits for its completion interrupt. While
it waits the CPUs go idle, and on SoCs with deep cluster and system
idle states each message then also pays the time to leave them. On
MT6789 those states take 1.05 to 4.1 ms to exit. A camera sensor
programmed through v4l2-cci writes one register per transfer, and
starting the Samsung S5KJN1 (about 300 register writes) took 0.3 to
2.6 s, varying with how deep the CPUs had gone, against about 0.2 s
with the deep states held off.

Hold a CPU latency request of 50 us for the duration of
mtk_i2c_transfer(), the value MediaTek's downstream kernels use for
this controller. spi-mt65xx does the same around its messages for the
same reason; i2c-omap once did it for OMAP3.

Signed-off-by: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-mt65xx.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-mt65xx.c b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-mt65xx.c
index 9e701b3..30fe7f0 100644
--- a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-mt65xx.c
+++ b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-mt65xx.c
@@ -21,6 +21,7 @@
 #include <linux/module.h>
 #include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/platform_device.h>
+#include <linux/pm_qos.h>
 #include <linux/scatterlist.h>
 #include <linux/sched.h>
 #include <linux/slab.h>
@@ -85,6 +86,9 @@
 
 #define I2C_DRV_NAME		"i2c-mt65xx"
 
+/* Wake-up latency the CPUs may take while a transfer waits for its interrupt */
+#define I2C_CPU_LATENCY_US	50
+
 /**
  * enum i2c_mt65xx_clks - Clocks enumeration for MT65XX I2C
  *
@@ -308,6 +312,7 @@ struct mtk_i2c {
 	bool ignore_restart_irq;
 	struct mtk_i2c_ac_timing ac_timing;
 	const struct mtk_i2c_compatible *dev_comp;
+	struct pm_qos_request cpu_latency;
 };
 
 /**
@@ -1262,6 +1267,8 @@ static int mtk_i2c_transfer(struct i2c_adapter *adap,
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+	cpu_latency_qos_add_request(&i2c->cpu_latency, I2C_CPU_LATENCY_US);
+
 	i2c->auto_restart = i2c->dev_comp->auto_restart;
 
 	/* checking if we can skip restart and optimize using WRRD mode */
@@ -1314,6 +1321,7 @@ static int mtk_i2c_transfer(struct i2c_adapter *adap,
 	ret = num;
 
 err_exit:
+	cpu_latency_qos_remove_request(&i2c->cpu_latency);
 	clk_bulk_disable(I2C_MT65XX_CLK_MAX, i2c->clocks);
 	return ret;
 }
-- 
